# Dev Toolbar Branch Protection

## Rule

The dev toolbar and all dev-only files must NEVER be merged, committed, cherry-picked, or pushed to the `main` branch.

## Dev-only files (listed in `.dev-only`)

- `js/dev-toolbar.js` — the toolbar itself
- `.dev-only` — the manifest
- `merge-to-main.sh` — the safe merge script

## The dev-toolbar import in `js/main.js`

The line `import("./dev-toolbar.js")` must be REMOVED before any code reaches `main`.

## When merging dev-preview → main

ALWAYS use `merge-to-main.sh` which automatically:
1. Merges without committing
2. Removes all `.dev-only` listed files
3. Strips the dev-toolbar import from `js/main.js`

NEVER do a direct `git merge dev-preview` on main. NEVER manually commit dev-only files on main.

## Safety layers in place

1. **pre-commit hook** — blocks commits on main containing dev-only files
2. **pre-push hook** — blocks pushes from main if dev-only files exist
3. **localhost guard** — the import only runs on localhost anyway
4. **This rule** — reminds the AI agent to never include dev files on main
